course: dictionary
lesson: 784
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. The word bed is a good example. Most of the time you think of a thing you sleep on, but the word also names a patch of soil for plants and the ground at the bottom of a river or sea.
explain: To work out which meaning is right, read the words around it. «Ruby stops games an hour before bed now» tells you bed means bedtime, the time you go to sleep. «Then she put it on the kitchen table and went to bed» means she went to sleep, not that she lay on a bunk.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. If it fits, you have probably got it. A flower bed is the place where you plant flowers, so it cannot be somewhere you sleep. Clues like flower, river or sea point to the right meaning.
fact: Bed can be a noun or a verb. As a noun it is a thing or a place, and as a verb it can mean to sleep somewhere, as in bed down.
fact: A bed is furniture you sleep on.
fact: A flower bed is a patch of ground where plants grow.
fact: The bed of a river or sea is the ground at its bottom.
fact: «Go to bed» means go to sleep at night, and «bedtime» is the time you do this.
exercise: «Ruby stops games an hour before bed now.» What does bed mean here? | *Bedtime, the time to go to sleep at night | A soft mattress in a shop | The ground at the bottom of a river | A patch of ground for plants
exercise: «The children planted tulips in the new flower bed.» What is a flower bed? | A bench for sitting on in the park | *A patch of ground for plants | A small tent for camping
exercise: A fish swam slowly along the bed of the river. What does bed mean here? | *The ground at the bottom of the river | Go to sleep | A flower patch | A soft mattress
test: «Sleepwalking is dangerous, so it is best to guide the child gently back to bed.» What does bed mean here? | To go to sleep for an hour | A flower patch in the garden | The ground at the bottom of the sea | *The furniture you sleep on
test: «Then she put it on the kitchen table and went to bed.» What does went to bed mean? | Sat down for a rest on the sofa | Lay down on the seabed | *Went to sleep | Went to the garden to plant seeds
exam: Which phrase uses bed to mean a patch of ground for plants? | Bunk bed | Make the bed | *Flower bed | Bedtime
